detaileddescription.para:
The weak integral element is $ w (\alpha 
abla B_i \cdot G^{-1} 
abla B_j +  eta B_i B_j) $ where $ w $ is the integral volume, $ B_i $ is the test function and $ B_j $ is the trial function. This function computes $ w \alpha G^{-1} 
abla B_i $ and $ w  eta B_i $ so that the weak integral element can be computed from the values and derivatives of the trial function alone.
